    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d191">

                <pb facs="0286" n="180" sameAs="frus:frus1933-39/pg180"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">121.5561/23: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wiley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-02-07T18:00:00+03:00">February 7, 1935—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 7—11:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>54. Your 27, February 6, 2 p.m., have notified Foreign Office as instructed. Your
                    26, February 6, 1 p.m. As Captain Nimmer’s orders provide for his departure
                    within the next few days I have requested <pb facs="0287" n="181" xml:id="pg181"
                    /> through the Foreign Office farewell interview with Voroshilov for both Nimmer
                    and White explaining in note that office of Naval Attaché has been abolished and
                    that latter is to be withdrawn.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wiley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
